{"id": 13, "ts": 1780654202.9384222, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s confidence in Candidate\u202fC\u2019s reliability and quick decision\u2011making, but the gaps in critical safety\u2011related evidence make me hesitant to endorse him as the sole choice. We have solid data that Candidate\u202fB is very conscientious (reliable), handles stress well, and possesses strong technical competence (weather assessment, computer skills). However, his nasty remarks and pretentious tone raise serious concerns for crew cooperation and professional communication\u2014key for long\u2011haul flights. Candidate\u202fA shows excellent technical and cognitive ability (complex connections, spatial vision) and very good leadership, yet we lack any reliability or stress\u2011handling evidence, and his \u201cshow\u2011off\u201d attitude could undermine teamwork. Candidate\u202fD demonstrates responsibility, adequate stress response, and strong problem\u2011solving and concentration, but his hot temper and \u201cknow\u2011it\u2011all\u201d reputation threaten crew cooperation. Given that Candidate\u202fC\u2019s technical competence, stress resilience, responsibility, and adaptability remain undocumented, I cannot weigh his reliability advantage against these unknowns. Therefore, I currently recommend **Candidate\u202fB** as the best overall fit, provided we can mitigate his communication style, because he offers the most complete evidence across reliability, stress resilience, and technical competence."}
